/T (As Karl Polanyi argues in The Great Transformation, the idea that economic life originates in isolated individuals engaging in exchange, is in fact historically unfounded. Economic systems, for most of the human history, were organised through reciprocity, redistribution, and householding and not through markets, and certainly not through self maximising individuals. Exchange did exist, but it did not give rise to markets, nor did it produce individualism. .)
/E (As Karl Polanyi argues in The Great Transformation, the idea that economic life originates in isolated individuals engaging in exchange, is in fact historically unfounded. Economic systems, for most of the human history, were organised through reciprocity, redistribution, and householding and not through markets, and certainly not through self maximising individuals. Exchange did exist, but it did not give rise to markets, nor did it produce individualism. .)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
