1092 0 obj
<<
/Title (The individual, therefore, is not a natural starting point, but instead a constructed abstraction, which becomes plausible only when the social conditions that produce it are obscured. To begin with this abstraction, and to build models upon it, is to misidentify the object of analysis from the outset.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1080 0 R
/Next 1106 0 R
>>
